peer:
But the flying sea-gulls wail;
I peer through the darkness that wraps the shore,
For sight of a home set sail.

peeled:
And ‘enter’ there; the points for clapping, fixed,
Like Jacob’s white-peeled rods before the rams;
And all the close-curled imagery clipped

peered:
I woke-and the scoffer may doubt me--
I peered in surprise through the gloom;
But nothing and none were about me,

Something scratched on the window-sill.
A pinched brown face peered in--I shivered;
No one listened or seemed to see;

peek:
With their parasols of green
Take a little peek at you;
They’re the bluest you have seen.

peepers:
Woo-oo, woo-oo!
Hide yo' little peepers 'hind yo' han;
Woo-oo, woo-oo!

peerless:
As I, with all my blots: with all my blots!
At last then, peerless cousin, we are peers—
At last we’re even. Ah, you’ve left your height;
